Z||000011||88CoupeV6||08-03-2001||12:31 PM||||May I suggest the Crane Hi-6. About the same price and adjusting the rev limiter is as easy as turning the knob. I've noticed lots more power from the car too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000012||Capt Fiero||08-03-2001||12:50 PM||||Some people say yes, but as easy as it is to build a tach filter, (one capacitor and one resistor, then crimp em together and put spade connectors on either end then wrap the package up nicly) I think I am rather happy having a tach filter. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||88CoupeV6||08-03-2001||01:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Capt Fiero:<BR><B>Some people say yes, but as easy as it is to build a tach filter, (one capacitor and one resistor, then crimp em together and put spade connectors on either end then wrap the package up nicly) I think I am rather happy having a tach filter. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know the crane Hi-6 has a tach output wire that you use. the box also has different tach test modes to see how well your tach works and how high it sweeps.<P>||||reg||1
